{"chunk_id": "910de3176f6e", "text": "The Pandavas, still living in disguise with their mother Kunti, decide to leave their current shelter and travel to the kingdom of Panchala, whose king Drupada is known for honoring Brahmanas. Before their departure, the sage Vyasa visits and tells them a prophetic story: in a previous life a maiden asked Shiva five times for a perfect husband, and as a result she is destined to have five husbands in her next birth. Vyasa reveals that this woman has been reborn as Krishna (Draupadi), daughter of Drupada, and that she will become the wife of all five Pandavas. On their journey northward they encounter the Gandharva Angaraparna at the Ganga. Arjuna defies him, defeats him with a celestial weapon, but spares his life at Yudhishthira\u2019s command. Grateful, the Gandharva offers Arjuna mystical knowledge and celestial horses, highlighting the themes of destiny, restraint, and honor.\nVyasa prophesies that Draupadi will marry all five Pandavas; later Arjuna defeats the Gandharva Angaraparna at the Ganga and spares his life.\nThemes: prophecy of Draupadi's marriage, fate and past-life karma, warrior honor and mercy, journey to Panchala, divine knowledge exchange", "vector": [-0.0008186153718270361, -0.037824809551239014, -0.010086615569889545, 0.015116510912775993, 0.0037623613607138395, 0.027604062110185623, -0.025793300941586494, -0.000923824030905962, -0.020186644047498703, -0.02002568729221821, 0.013050900772213936, 0.018885578960180283, 0.0050198351964354515, 0.012152225710451603, 0.001847648061811924, 0.022091297432780266, 0.043109551072120667, -0.01632368564605713, 0.02666514925658703, -0.027765018865466118, -0.007826516404747963, -0.0028620101511478424, 0.0023372245486825705, 0.009456202387809753, -0.030796369537711143, 0.028247889131307602, 0.02022688463330269, -0.007658853195607662, 0.0019532758742570877, -0.011917497962713242, -0.017544273287057877, 0.004416247829794884, -0.009268419817090034, 0.0004635886289179325, -0.030